WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.580
Why is Turing-recognizable the same

2
00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.300
as enumerable? A recognizer answers

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.940
membership positively, while an enumerator

4
00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:09.380
prints language members from a

5
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.840
blank start. The equivalence relies

6
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.340
on a fair schedule so

7
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.200
a nonhalting test never prevents

8
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:16.960
later strings from being generated.

9
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.200
An enumerator may print words

10
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.800
in arbitrary order and may

11
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.840
repeat them. Its language is

12
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:23.980
the set of strings it

13
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.720
ever prints, not the set

14
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.540
of all intermediate tape contents.

15
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.940
It may run forever, print

16
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.760
finitely many words, or print

17
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.280
nothing for the empty language.

18
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.560
For equal zero and one

19
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.700
blocks, a direct enumerator is

20
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.580
simple. Let n start at

21
00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.820
zero, print n zeros followed

22
00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.840
by n ones, increment n

23
00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.020
and repeat. The outputs begin

24
00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.500
epsilon, zero one, zero zero

25
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:50.300
one one, with each language

26
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.940
member printed once because its

27
00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:52.840
n is unique.

28
00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:56.440
For the general enumerator-to-recognizer direction,

29
00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.460
take the input word w

30
00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:01.580
and simulate the enumerator. Whenever

31
00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.560
a string is printed, compare

32
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.340
it with w and accept

33
00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:07.240
if they match. If w

34
00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.420
is never printed, the recognizer

35
00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.100
may wait forever, which is

36
00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.440
permitted for a nonmember.

37
00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:14.940
For the other direction, list

38
00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.520
all input strings in shortlex

39
00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.900
order and consider a recognizer

40
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.720
on each. Running them one

41
00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.820
after another is unsafe, because

42
00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.520
the first nonmember might make

43
00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:26.860
its recognizer loop. Instead at

44
00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.760
stage t, simulate the first

45
00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:30.160
t inputs for t steps

46
00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:31.960
each and print any that

47
00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:32.540
have accepted.

48
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.700
Every member has some finite

49
00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.900
index j and some finite

50
00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.480
accepting time k. Once a

51
00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.060
stage reaches at least both

52
00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.120
j and k, its accepting

53
00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.740
run is included and has

54
00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:46.600
enough steps, so that word

55
00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.860
is printed. No nonmember is

56
00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:50.860
printed because a correct recognizer

57
00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:51.980
never accepts one.

58
00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.640
These bounded simulations can restart

59
00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:56.240
from scratch each stage without

60
00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.240
changing the existence argument. A

61
00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.100
more efficient implementation may retain

62
00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.320
partial runs instead, but fairness

63
00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.220
is the essential property. Never

64
00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:05.780
let a possibly infinite run

65
00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:07.560
occupy the only simulation slot

66
00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.040
forever.

67
00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:10.120
If the language is decidable,

68
00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.080
its decider halts on every

69
00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.240
tested word, so serial shortlex

70
00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:16.360
testing becomes safe. Print a

71
00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:17.900
word exactly when the decider

72
00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.540
accepts and then continue to

73
00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.800
the next word. This produces

74
00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.500
members once in string order

75
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:26.000
without needing the general recognizable-language

76
00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.280
dovetailing construction.

77
00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:31.120
The converse sorted-enumeration characterization needs

78
00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:33.000
a small qualification in its

79
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.080
proof. For an infinite language

80
00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:36.960
printed in strict shortlex order,

81
00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.040
waiting until w appears or

82
00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.600
a larger word appears decides

83
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:43.020
membership. A finite language is

84
00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:44.840
decidable by a fixed finite

85
00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:46.900
table; blindly waiting for a

86
00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.520
larger printed word could otherwise

87
00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.960
hang after the last output.

88
00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:51.720
Things to take note of.

89
00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:54.440
Distinguish printing from tape contents,

90
00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.960
allow repetition and arbitrary order

91
00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.820
in the general definition, and

92
00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.960
prove eventual printing using finite

93
00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.240
index and finite accepting time.

94
00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:06.320
Sorted enumeration uses stronger ordering

95
00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:08.800
information, while a mere recognizer

96
00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.360
cannot be run serially on

97
00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:11.560
all candidates safely.
